  "query_preview": "(This evening through Sunday)...\nIssued at 232 PM EDT Sun Oct 25 2026\n\nRest of This Afternoon through Tuesday...\n\nHigh clouds and some mid clouds will continue to spill across an \nupper ridge through Tuesday, bringing partly cloudy conditions at \ntimes. \n\nThe ridge itself will get pushed south a bit by upper waves well to \nthe north of the local area. This will allow a surface cold front to \nsag south into central Indiana later Monday into Monday night. This \nfront will get pulled back north as a low pressure system moves into \nMinnesota on Tuesday. With minimal moisture and little or no \nforcing, no rain is expected with the front.\n\nThe cooler air behind the front most likely won't reach into central \nIndiana. Thus, expect highs in the 70s to continue with lows in the \n40s. Patchy ground fog will develop near sunrise Monday and Tuesday \nwith light winds continuing. The fog may be muted by thicker cloud \ncover though.\n\nWednesday through Friday...\n\nA weakening upper wave will move northeast into the lower Great \nLakes Wednesday. This may bring additional clouds but again forcing \nand moisture across central Indiana will be low enough to continue a \ndry forecast.\n\nA surface cold front will try and work south Thursday and Friday. \nGuidance differs on how far south this front gets by late Friday. \nWith upper flow generally west to southwest ahead of another upper \nwave, feel that the front will likely remain north of the area. Will \ncontinue a dry forecast and go with the warmer guidance. \n\nThis means that highs will continue to be in the 70s, with perhaps \nsome upper 70s for parts of the area.\n\nHalloween Weekend...\n\nAny lingering upper ridging will exit as multiple upper troughs move \nthrough next weekend. Uncertainty remains high on the details, but \nfor now it appears that the best forcing and moisture will arrive \novernight Saturday night into Sunday morning, with only low chances \nfor rain during Halloween evening events.\n\nIf the front remains north, highs will be in the 70s. However, a \nmore southern front as well as any rain would keep readings lower, \nespecially on Sunday.",
